    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0290" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/8–2144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-21T20:00:00+02:00">August 21, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 21—3:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6763. Comea 75. The Russian Ambassador just called and left me a letter<anchor
                        n="26" xml:id="d149-f1"/> stating that his Government has resolved to
                    confirm the terms of unconditional surrender for Germany agreed and signed by
                    the European Advisory Commission on July 25.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
